A||||5||86SE||Talk about the right place at the right time!||||6||
Z||000000||86SE||08-08-2001||01:12 AM||||I was in Emery's local shop today getting my rear brakes on the Fiero fixed when I mentioned my rod knock and putting a new motor in.  Roger, the shop owner, overhears this and i start talking to him about it.  I told him i was looking for a pushrod V6 from a 93-95 Camaro or Firebird.<P>He was like "So what years now?"  so i told him, "Camaro or Firebird did ya say?"  Me "Yep".  Then he said he will be right back, he went into his office and got on the phone, motioned for me to come in so I did.  He started telling me what to write down.<P>He found a '93 Camaro motor with 80,000 miles for $425 and a '94 Firebird motor with 18,000 for $750!  I'll take the low mileage one!  Gonna go down tomorrow to pay for it.  Finally got my self an engine and its only 40 miles from my house!<P>Thought i would share my luck, im still a little excited!!<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://fierodude.hypermart.net/mysig.jpg">  <BR>'86 Special Edition,<BR>High-Output V-6 Yellow Fiero -- 3.4L Conversion *Back in session!* --||||reg||6
Z||000001||sqoach||08-08-2001||01:21 AM||||Wow! What luck! Glad to hear it.<BR>I wouldn't mind doing a 3.4 when I get the time and money. Should be fun  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR><FONT COLOR="BLUE">sqoach@yahoo.com</FONT><BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sqoach.gif">   <P>84 SE (FOR SALE)*sale pending*<BR>85 Coupe (parts car)($50)*sale pending*<BR>86 SC (FOR SALE)<BR>86 SE V6 (new project)||||reg||14
Z||000002||AusFiero||08-08-2001||02:19 AM||||Just out of interest, is the 3.4 a bolt in operation? Or does it need adapting? If so, what has to be done?<P>Hadn't considered that option if it is easy.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.auto-alley.com" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||202.139.20.3||reg||1
Z||000003||86SE||08-08-2001||02:42 AM||||The pushrod 3.4L is a 'bold-it' upgrade as in it bolts to the tranny and accepts all Fiero dress up parts and accessories, so it will look like the factory 2.8.  The main modification that has to be done to the 3.4 block is the relocation of the starter, so you have to redrill and tap new starter holes to mount the starter on the other side of the engine.<P>I was told its pretty much a straight foreward swap, so im gonna give it a shot.<P>Chuck||||reg||1
Z||000004||Songman||08-08-2001||03:01 AM||||What about motor mounts? I thought they had to be changed...<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Raydar||08-08-2001||07:41 AM||||This is the page I always send people to, for 3.4 swap info. Ed Parks' Fiero Factory... <A HREF="http://www.angelfire.com/on/fierofactory/start.html#34" TARGET=_blank>http://www.angelfire.com/on/fierofactory/start.html#34</A> <P>Very minor mods. <P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||14
